{"id":637,"flavor":[{"games":["Shield"],"text":"This Pokémon emerges from a cocoon formed of raging flames. Ancient murals depict Volcarona as a deity of fire."},{"games":["Sword"],"text":"Volcarona scatters burning scales. Some say it does this to start fires. Others say it’s trying to rescue those that suffer in the cold."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"According to legends, it was hatched from a flaming cocoon to save people and Pokémon that were suffering from the cold."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"As it flies, it scatters its flaming scales. It was feared by ancient people, who referred to it as “the rage of the sun.”"},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Y","Black"],"text":"When volcanic ash darkened the atmosphere, it is said that Volcarona’s fire provided a replacement for the sun."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","X","White"],"text":"A sea of fire engulfs the surroundings of their battles, since they use their six wings to scatter their ember scales."},{"games":["White 2","Black 2"],"text":"Thought to be an embodiment of the sun, it appeared during a bitterly cold winter and saved Pokémon from freezing."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Flame Body","hidden":false,"description":"Contact with the Pokémon may burn the attacker."},{"name":"Swarm","hidden":true,"description":"Powers up Bug-type moves when the Pokémon's HP is low."}],"eggGroups":["Bug"],"genderRate":4,"hatchCounter":40,"baseHappiness":70,"growthRate":"slow","habitat":null,"color":"White","shape":"Bug wings","evolution":{"id":636,"name":"Larvesta","condition":null,"children":[{"id":637,"name":"Volcarona","condition":"Lv. 59","children":[]}]},"moves":{"game":"Scarlet / Violet","level":[[0,483],[1,16],[1,18],[1,36],[1,38],[1,52],[1,81],[1,83],[1,394],[1,488],[1,522],[1,552],[18,172],[24,450],[30,103],[36,141],[42,405],[48,257],[54,133],[62,542],[70,126],[78,476]],"machine":[512,314,403,133,34,450,405,347,38,814,203,263,126,83,488,53,394,19,202,416,257,542,63,141,113,679,315,398,884,182,94,240,156,806,214,76,522,164,24